From bb3f1aee1420b69d471f3ef157e7a2dcf0a85705 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Balister <philip@balister.org>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:07:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] magnitude_32f: Refine the NEON square root

volk_32fc_magnitude_32f_neon computed sqrt as vrecpeq_f32(vrsqrteq_f32(x))
with no refinement step. Both instructions are estimates accurate to
about 8 bits, so the kernel's results are off by up to 0.5%: |2+1i| comes
out as 2.2343750 instead of 2.2360680. This is the failure in GNU Radio's
qa_type_conversions on a ZCU104, whose volk_config selects this kernel.
The kernel test doesn't catch it, since its tolerance is 1e-1 to allow
for neon_fancy_sweet's approximation (about 1%).

Use _vsqrtq_f32, which refines the reciprocal square root estimate with
two Newton-Raphson steps and works on ARMv7 NEON, which has no
vsqrtq_f32.

volk_test_all volk_32fc_magnitude_32f, max relative error of neon vs
generic, aarch64 (cortex-a57) under qemu-user:
  before: 5.3e-03
  after:  2.4e-07 (neonv8: 1.2e-07)

+0, +Inf and inputs whose squared magnitude overflows to +Inf give the
same results as generic.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/gnuradio/volk/pull/886]
Signed-off-by: Philip Balister <philip@balister.org>
---
 kernels/volk/volk_32fc_magnitude_32f.h | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernels/volk/volk_32fc_magnitude_32f.h b/kernels/volk/volk_32fc_magnitude_32f.h
index dadcc31..11ae24f 100644
--- a/kernels/volk/volk_32fc_magnitude_32f.h
+++ b/kernels/volk/volk_32fc_magnitude_32f.h
@@ -406,6 +406,7 @@ static inline void volk_32fc_magnitude_32f_a_sse(float* magnitudeVector,
 
 #ifdef LV_HAVE_NEON
 #include <arm_neon.h>
+#include <volk/volk_neon_intrinsics.h>
 
 static inline void volk_32fc_magnitude_32f_neon(float* magnitudeVector,
                                                 const lv_32fc_t* complexVector,
@@ -423,8 +424,10 @@ static inline void volk_32fc_magnitude_32f_neon(float* magnitudeVector,
         complex_vec.val[0] = vmulq_f32(complex_vec.val[0], complex_vec.val[0]);
         magnitude_vec =
             vmlaq_f32(complex_vec.val[0], complex_vec.val[1], complex_vec.val[1]);
-        magnitude_vec = vrsqrteq_f32(magnitude_vec);
-        magnitude_vec = vrecpeq_f32(magnitude_vec); // no plain ol' sqrt
+        // ARMv7 NEON has no vsqrtq_f32; _vsqrtq_f32 refines the reciprocal
+        // square root estimate with Newton-Raphson steps. The bare estimates
+        // are only accurate to about 8 bits.
+        magnitude_vec = _vsqrtq_f32(magnitude_vec);
         vst1q_f32(magnitudeVectorPtr, magnitude_vec);
 
         complexVectorPtr += 8;
-- 
